# GateRail delivery-gate Stop hook — check configuration.
#
# One check per line: <cwd> <TAB> <command>
# - <cwd> is relative to the project root this file lives under.
# - <command> runs via `eval`, so shell operators (&&, |, etc.) work.
# - Lines starting with '#', and blank lines, are ignored.
#
# This file is NOT auto-enabled — rename it to gaterail-checks.txt (dropping
# .example) only after filling in commands that actually exist in this
# repository. An empty or missing gaterail-checks.txt means the hook is a
# no-op; a wrong command in here means every turn gets blocked on a
# false failure. Find the real command with
# ../references/discovering-project-checks.md, verify it passes on a clean
# checkout first, then add it here.
#
# Examples (uncomment and adapt — do not leave these as literal defaults):
# .    npm test
# .    pytest
# examples/ts-cli    npm run build && npm run typecheck && npm test
